#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0552 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "dataset ADLBC structure=BDS. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), PARAMCD(Char), MCRIT1MN(Num). ONE row: `CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 1`. MCRIT1MN is declared, MCRIT1ML is NOT a column of the table at all - that absence is the violation. Wildcard: `MCRITyMN` matches MCRIT1MN so the tuple y=1 is seeded; `MCRITyML` has no matching column and its concrete name MCRIT1ML is synthesised as absent, giving the single expansion `var_exists('MCRIT1MN') and not var_exists('MCRIT1ML')` = TRUE. Presence Check -> dataset granularity -> exactly ONE violation."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt nameOnly=MCRIT1MN
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col MCRIT1MN type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 1
